  - So a cushion of about 1.1–1.2× is close to ideal. Candidate 1 loses on shortages and penalties.\n- **Candidate 4 (orders every 4 days):** it pays 6 fewer order fees, about 350 saved. But on average it holds roughly 55 more units, which costs about 900 in storage over the month. Its large deliveries (one is 163 + 72 units) also come close to the 208-unit warehouse limit. Net, it is worse.\n- **Candidate 6 (orders every 3 days):** it saves about 230 in fees but pays about 440 more in storage. It does carry a cushion of about 1.1×, so it may be close to candidate 1. That pair is my least certain call.\n- **Candidate 5 (orders daily):** it pays 13 more order fees (about 750) and saves only about 440 in storage. It also orders roughly exactly the forecast with no cushion, so it runs short often.\n\nThe first days are short for every plan, since the starting stock does not cover demand until the first deliveries arrive. So that does not separate the candidates."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5048, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5048}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T08:17:00.638Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWCPfUdDzfNXoYqa1RiX"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_011kSZ8uDrBut3XswLnhKKcG", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgWCPfjkhmtwJ9JtK9k